WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.570
If this continues,

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.870
there will be more rag demons in our future
rising up to oppose mankind.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.700
You're so cute, Mugaro!

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.210
I hope he comes back soon.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.670
The child unleashed his power
this afternoon.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.920
Would you have been this much of
a pathetic crybaby ten years ago?

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.010
There has to be a path where
all three races can live in peace!

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.840
And I will never give up on it!

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.390
You live your life your way.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.220
I will be doing what I feel is right.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.480
Pervert!

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.040
Here.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:00.300
Nina, is this okay?

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:05.050
Nina?

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.550
Stop bothering me, pervert.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.520
Young lady...

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.900
Please remember how Bacchus
kindly opened up his home

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:20.070
to provide you a place to stay
when you had nowhere else to turn.

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:21.570
Whatever.

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:24.450
I think that's a bit cruel to dismiss.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.950
Nina, we don't have enough chili peppers
and chicken wings.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.200
Could you go buy some?

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:30.870
Okay.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:38.250
You're making chicken wings again
this year? They were a big hit last year.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.210
I should've bought more.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.050
Nina will be in quite the predicament
if that handsome man

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.670
shows up and we're out of wings.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:50.180
Yes, you're right. If that handsome man
you arm wrestled shows up,

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.060
we've got to let him try some.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:53.640
Hey, cut that out!

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.890
What's this man you're talking about?
Nobody told me about him!

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.940
He sure was a handsome man.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:02.440
He had a noble dignity about him.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.400
-I hope he comes.
-I'm off, then!

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.700
Did you know, Rita?

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:21.920
Nina still keeps the ring that the man
left behind that day in her pocket.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:24.880
My, how girly of her.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:28.930
It wasn't that long ago that she was
blushing from Azazel.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.890
The heart is a fickle thing.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.700
Rage of Bahamut

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:16.580
There has to be a path where
all three races can live in peace!

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:18.790
And I will never give up on it!

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:33.970
-Thanks!
-Oh, Nina!

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.890
I baked some bread for the celebration!
Why don't you take a loaf?

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:39.390
Really?

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:44.980
And these aren't your usual leftovers.
This is hot and fresh!

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:48.570
Yay, thanks a lot!

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:57.240
Stop right there.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.960
You again? What do you want?

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:09.000
I promised didn't I?
I'm here to make you my slave.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.650
No! My meat!

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:46.790
What's wrong? Can't do anything
when you're on your own?

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.130
Stop it!

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:53.800
She's still just a child!

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:03.640
I hate my body so much!

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:06.270
Who the hell do you think you are?

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:24.250
-Damn you!
-Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:25.870
Take this!

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.040
That's...

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:41.640
Come on, let's go.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:59.490
Oh, God. This is bad.
This is bad. This is so bad.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.760
Not only are you strong,
but you're fast as well.

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:30.140
Why did you not fight back?

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:31.900
That's...

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:34.610
Because I'm a girl...

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:36.820
Why are you looking down?

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:41.030
Nina, was it?

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:46.120
You remembered.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:48.830
Did you need something from me?

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:56.210
Tonight is the night before Anatae's
big festival, right?

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:00.880
I'll be running a food stand with a friend.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:05.640
I want to thank you for helping me,
so would you come by?

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:08.890
You'll know it from the carriage
when we arm wrestled.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:11.060
I see. Very well.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:18.530
"I see. Very well," huh?

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:29.500
"I see. Very well."

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.040
"I see. Very well."

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:37.500
What took you so long?

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:44.800
What happened to these peppers?

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:46.140
Where's the meat?

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:47.470
I dropped it.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:48.930
You dropped it?

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:51.140
Then why didn't you just pick it up?

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:52.480
Oh, right.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:56.480
-It got stepped on!
-By who?

00:08:56.940 --> 00:08:58.480
By bad people.

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:00.070
What?

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:01.690
Sorry!

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:03.650
Whatever.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:06.490
I'll have to make do
with these sad peppers.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:08.990
I guess these
are all the wings we'll have.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:14.670
Perhaps she's shocked
from dropping the chicken wings.

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:20.000
I know what I told him,
but what if he really shows up?

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:24.760
I'll turn into a dragon. I just know I will!

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:26.680
He'll come. He won't.

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:28.470
He'll come. He won't.

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:30.390
He'll come. He won't.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:34.310
What are you doing? Stop that please!

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:37.560
What am I doing?

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:40.770
This is terrible!

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:46.860
Your Majesty!

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:50.870
Where have you been?

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:56.040
You must tell one of us
when you decide to leave the palace.

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:58.000
Quiet.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:07.720
Tomorrow afternoon, the humans
will be putting on a parade.

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:10.970
The parade will begin
from the castle gates,

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:14.730
proceed down the center of the city,
make its way around the plaza,

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:16.190
and return to the castle.

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:19.310
The crucial point will be here.

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:22.610
The parade will need to be
stopped here first.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:27.400
I will use that as a signal to come down
from the north here with the red dragon.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:29.160
A pincer attack?

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:34.700
The soldiers in black armor should prove
the most troublesome.

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:37.540
I will draw them to the red dragon.

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:40.290
While I do, you will split up into two groups

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:44.380
and attack the remaining troops
and their king.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.760
The first squad will conduct a range attack
from high ground.

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:52.300
The second squad will engage in
close combat and slay the king!

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:58.560
But this plan
relies heavily on the red dragon.

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:04.110
All we can do is trust you.
There's no room for failure.

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.570
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:11:13.450 --> 00:11:19.670
Rage of Bahamut

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:35.810
The town's so festive...

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:39.350
Apart from us, that is.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:43.440
How's that make you feel, Captain?

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:48.440
You live your life your way.

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:52.410
I will be doing what I feel is right.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:11.130
Dias, I am leaving you in charge!

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:15.430
There he goes off on his own again.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:47.040
Welcome, welcome!
We have delicious wings!

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:50.550
But mine taste even better,
not that I'll let you eat me!

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:53.380
We'll run out if you draw that many in.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.390
Come on in!

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:58.850
Nina, stop spacing out. It's dangerous.

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:00.310
Okay.

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:05.730
Welcome, welcome!
Our spicy wings are to die for!

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:08.570
Nina, are you okay?

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:10.900
Would you leave me alone please?

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:14.030
Now, now! These wings are perfect

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:17.240
for a festive night like this!
They'll light a fire in your belly!

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:20.910
Oh, hey there, young man!
Good to see you again!

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:28.420
This is the handsome guy
from the arm wrestling we mentioned.

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:31.340
He's not bad.

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:38.260
I forgot to return one to you.

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:44.480
Welcome!

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:46.150
Hey there, youngblood.

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:47.810
What?

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:52.820
What are you doing, Bacchus?

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:55.070
Our wings are great,

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:57.160
but this is the last of our special.

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:00.950
Are you sure you want me to have it?

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:02.160
Of course!

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:04.370
But would you do me a favor

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:07.790
and take this girl
around to see the festival with you?

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:10.960
She's got a big chest for her age.

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:16.510
-You're so stupid.
-Very well.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:18.840
Say what now?

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:21.010
We can go after I finish this.

00:14:57.550 --> 00:14:59.430
Would you like one?

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:08.100
You are supposed to peel it first.

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:12.940
I knew that! Of course I knew that.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:16.440
It's so good!

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:11.830
Are you sure about this?

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.170
It doesn't matter how great he is.

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:17.960
This is her first time
going out alone with a boy.

00:16:18.130 --> 00:16:21.170
She might come back all grown up!

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:22.340
Hey!

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:25.100
You're the one who put them up to it!

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:29.310
You'd better hope she doesn't turn into
a dragon in the middle of the festival.

00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:46.410
Would you like to try?

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:51.540
No way, I can't.
I don't know this dance at all.

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:15.540
How was I able to dance like that?

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:20.840
I got so close to him,
and we even held hands.

00:18:21.590 --> 00:18:23.170
No, no, no!

00:18:23.340 --> 00:18:26.380
I haven't danced like that
since I was a child.

00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:28.840
You were quite good.

00:18:30.550 --> 00:18:32.890
It did not feel like your first time.

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:35.230
Really?

00:18:35.390 --> 00:18:38.730
That was the first time
I've danced with a man,

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:42.230
and the first time I've been out alone
in the city with one like this.

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:43.400
Me as well.

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:47.200
Yeah, right!
You were so good at dancing.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:53.120
I know how to dance, but I have never
walked around the city with a lady before.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:57.210
It was fun.

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:09.590
Could you tell me your name?

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:13.140
My name? My name is

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:14.930
Chris.

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:16.890
Chris.

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:19.440
Will I see you again?

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:22.610
I want to dance with you again.

00:19:22.770 --> 00:19:25.400
I don't know.

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:27.570
Why not?

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:29.650
I hope we can see each other again.

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:35.160
I hope we can see each other again.
I hope we can see each other again.

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:37.330
I hope we can see each other again.

00:20:01.060 --> 00:20:02.560
I'm so sorry!

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:04.820
Oh, it's you.

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:06.150
Who are you?

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:08.650
It's me.

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:12.450
Azazel! Where have you been?

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:14.950
How could you leave Mugaro like that?

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:16.160
The time has come.

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:19.120
What? What time?

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:23.830
When the parade begins tomorrow,
go to that tower there.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:26.710
Not that one, this one.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:29.050
Sorry.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:30.510
Promise me you'll be there.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:41.020
What was with his attitude?

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:52.360
You again.

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:55.320
What are you doing here?

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:57.740
Preparing for the festival.

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:00.250
What are you planning on doing?

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:05.880
You just wait.

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:10.170
We will be joining you
in your big day of celebration.

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:28.520
Dear Mom,
Something happened to me today.

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:32.440
I've never felt this way before.

00:21:33.280 --> 00:21:34.570
Could it be?

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:48.880
Is this love?

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:07.980
It's okay, it's okay
I cast the usual spell

00:22:08.150 --> 00:22:12.070
Stagnation, stagnation
My words and heart are at odds

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:15.950
Default
I've taken all the paint

00:22:16.110 --> 00:22:20.370
And mixed up all the colors
Until you're left with me

00:22:20.910 --> 00:22:22.870
So fragile
Yet strong

00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:25.000
Close to overflowing
But not spilling

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:29.000
Because I'm incomplete
I won't amount to much

00:22:29.170 --> 00:22:33.340
This is just a good luck charm
I'm not asking for your help

00:22:33.510 --> 00:22:37.340
This is just a good luck charm
I was just clinging to you

00:22:37.760 --> 00:22:45.890
Let's end it all today
I'm done living this pointless life

00:22:46.060 --> 00:22:54.990
Let's end it all today
I've taken my last pointless breath

00:22:55.690 --> 00:22:59.610
To whom it may concern
See ya and goodbye

00:22:59.780 --> 00:23:03.490
I killed the person I was yesterday

00:23:03.830 --> 00:23:10.500
To whom it may concern
See ya and goodbye

00:23:10.670 --> 00:23:14.340
A new morning is coming

00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:45.200
Let's go.

00:23:47.080 --> 00:23:49.210
Charioce!

00:23:49.370 --> 00:23:50.960
-Raggy!
-Raggy?

00:23:51.120 --> 00:23:53.380
Wasn't it uncomfortable to be wrapped
up so tight?

00:23:53.540 --> 00:23:55.840
-The rags stretch!
-Oh, right.

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:59.340
Next time on Rage of Bahamut:
Virgin Soul, "The Day of Victory."

00:23:59.510 --> 00:24:01.130
Raggy! Oh, never mind.

00:24:01.300 --> 00:24:04.010
Baha Soul!!

00:24:04.180 --> 00:24:05.890
Baha Baha Baha Soul!

00:24:06.430 --> 00:24:08.270
I demand you watch
the next episode.

00:24:08.430 --> 00:24:10.520
Don't you dare disappoint me.
